# netsurf: streaming transport -- XHR readyState 2/3 + progress, EventSource
#
# North-star blocker B1 (docs/north-star.md): responses reached JS only on
# completion (macos9_js_fetch.c set readyState straight to 4) and there was
# no EventSource, so nothing that streams -- SSE, progress bars, token-by-
# token model output -- could work.
#
# - macos9_js_fetch.c: FETCH_DATA schedules one progress tick per scheduler
#   pass (de-duplicated with macos9_sched_is_queued; a pass can carry many
#   curl writes). The tick sets status (always from the live fetch: after a
#   redirect it still held the 3xx), headers and responseURL, and calls the
#   object's __onNativeProgress(received). xhr_deliver runs a still-queued
#   tick first, so JS always sees 2 and 3 before 4.
# - __xhrNativeTake(id, discard): the body bytes since the last take, cut
#   at a UTF-8 boundary while the fetch is live (a split character would
#   decode to U+FFFD on both sides). JS pulls, so a page that never reads a
#   partial body copies nothing; discard=1 compacts the native buffer, so a
#   long-lived stream never grows towards the 4 MiB XHR cap.
# - XMLHttpRequest: open() fires readystatechange (OPENED); progress ticks
#   move to HEADERS_RECEIVED then LOADING with the partial responseText and
#   a progress event; DONE fires progress before load. lengthComputable /
#   total come from Content-Length (they were loaded>0 / loaded, telling a
#   progress bar it knew a stream's size). fetch()'s own XHR skips partial
#   copies (it resolves at DONE; streaming Response.body is the next step).
# - EventSource (vita_polyfill.js), replacing the always-failing stub: the
#   spec's parser (CRLF/LF/CR, BOM, comments, data joining, event, id with
#   Last-Event-ID on reconnect, retry), open on a 200 text/event-stream,
#   reconnect after the server closes, fail for good on an HTTP error or a
#   wrong Content-Type, close() aborts the native slot.
#
# testpages/pages/JS-streaming.html (NET-js-streaming{,-https}) checks all
# seven behaviours over http and https against tools/vita-sim/httpd.py's
# /progress-stream and /sse.
